{"title":"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 43","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_43&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Of the following statements, the only one that is incorrect is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/1/2016fdd031960fe0e0afaa3641d0e15a5de6b0e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\text{An inequality will remain true after each side is increased,}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"457\" height=\"17\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51dea9d6e3679f68ba0a1205894bba0886bf3fbe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ decreased, multiplied or divided zero excluded by the same positive quantity.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"564\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/5/705537896f46a7a856ea1454fb95c8517058682a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\text{The arithmetic mean of two unequal positive quantities is greater than their geometric mean.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"713\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/5/f358c7698e16e36a2e842d9eb97bcba6c44bd748.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\text{If the sum of two positive quantities is given, ther product is largest when they are equal.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"685\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/b/0ab4e2d144ac92041cb049e6899919de6beecd2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{If }a\\text{ and }b\\text{ are positive and unequal, }\\frac{1}{2}(a^{2}+b^{2})\\text{ is greater than }[\\frac{1}{2}(a+b)]^{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"587\" height=\"37\" /> \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6f55fe3047d901555e0592da53bebaf354d0326.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{If the product of two positive quantities is given, their sum is greatest when they are equal.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"698\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_43&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/f/6bfc0829f3f29bbf35d0a861644e00cfef0f50ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"39\" height=\"28\" />.\nQuite the opposite of statement (E) is true--the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> is <i>minimized</i> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5abd2c942ae299fd26e18d0ca5d390a7ca4a8c34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=b$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, but it approaches <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/7/b671f1bb7e4ee86584347d5d22f1dc8abdb5bef2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"9\" /> when one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bdf3e496517e8f8742f81dd774be1f93cf6e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> gets arbitrarily small.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_43&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME\" title=\"1951 AHSME\">1951 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1951 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1951\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_42\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 42\">Problem 42</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_44\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 44\">Problem 44</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_